 for the places where the site has readers.</p>
<h2>Information you provide</h2>
<p>The site does not currently offer user accounts, comments, a newsletter sign-up, or an on-site contact form. If you submit a correction or suggestion through the <a href="https://github.com/PureLight-web/WorldFoodCrisis/issues">public GitHub issue tracker</a>, the information you post is processed by GitHub and may be visible publicly. Do not post private, financial, health or other sensitive information in a public issue.</p>
<h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
<p>The site is delivered as a static website through Cloudflare Pages. The hosting and security infrastructure may process technical request information such as IP address, browser and device details, requested URLs, timestamps and security events to deliver pages, diagnose errors and protect the service. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a> for information about its handling of data.</p>
<h2>Google Analytics</h2>
<p>The website source currently includes Google Analytics 4 with measurement ID <code>G-3RNLG473FS</code>. Analytics can report page views, referring pages, general browser/device information and interactions, and may use cookies or similar technologies. Google's processing is subject to its own terms and privacy disclosures. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">Google Analytics' data safeguards</a>. Browser settings can restrict or clear cookies, although browser controls may not replace a legally required consent choice.</p>
<p>Before adding advertising or expanding analytics use, the publisher should assess consent requirements for the actual configuration and audience. Do not treat this notice alone as implementation of a consent mechanism.</p>
<h2>Advertising status</h2>
<p>As of 17 October 2026, the inspected website source does not contain an active AdSense ad tag. If advertising is activated, this notice should be updated to identify the relevant advertising services, cookies or similar technologies, data uses and available choices. Google requires a Google-certified consent management platform integrated with the IAB Transparency and Consent Framework when serving personalized ads to users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland; see <a href="https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/13554116">Google's consent-management requirements for publishers</a>. The publisher must also check the requirements that apply to other locations and products.</p>
<h2>External links, retention and choices</h2>
<p>Links to FAO, WFP, government agencies, publishers and other third parties take you to services with their own privacy practices. This static site does not provide a user account or on-site profile to delete. Information posted to third-party services is managed under those services' policies and settings. For a correction or question, see <a href="/contact/">Contact & Corrections</a>.</p>
<h2>Policy updates</h2>
<p>This notice should be reviewed whenever analytics, advertising, contact methods or hosting arrangements change. The review date above indicates when this page was checked; it is not a guarantee that every jurisdiction's legal requirements have been independently assessed.</p></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-main"><div class="footer-brand"><a class="brand brand-footer" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">F<span>+</span></span><span class="brand-words"><strong>World Food Crisis</strong><small>Facts before fear.</small></span></a><p>Independent explainers on food availability, prices and food security.</p></div><div class="footer-col"><strong>Explore</strong><a href="/data/">Data desk</a><a href="/sources/">Sources</a><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a></div><div class="footer-col"><strong>About</strong><a href="/about/">Our purpose</a><a href="/contact/">Corrections & contact</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></div></div><div class="container footer-bottom"><span>© <span data-year>2026</span> World Food Crisis</span><span>Sources over speculation.</span></div></footer></body></html>